Move a gradient with its shape when only the transform changes. Backported from ThorVG's
5b7b4c4c (in v1.1.0), which is below as it was committed.

The CPU engine bakes a shape's transform into its gradient's placement, and only worked that
out again when the gradient or colour changed. So a gradient in a scene that moved -- a
LiteWebView page, scrolled -- stayed where it was first drawn while its shape moved on, and
the shape showed the gradient's end colour, or its start, instead of the gradient. Drop this
patch when ThorVG is updated to v1.1.0 or later.

From 5b7b4c4cd9d94561d9200df20dcfa2de8edbf722 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nor-s <soongeon@lottiefiles.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 13:28:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] cpu_engine: fix outdated gradient fill on transform-only
 updates

The gradient placement coefficients baked in _prepareLinear/_prepareRadial
depend on the shape transform, but SwShapeTask::run's fill-update mask
ignored Transform, so in retained mode a transformed gradient stayed
pinned to its old position. Add Transform to regenerate the coefficients;
the color table stays gated on Gradient.
---
 src/renderer/cpu_engine/tvgSwRenderer.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/renderer/cpu_engine/tvgSwRenderer.cpp b/src/renderer/cpu_engine/tvgSwRenderer.cpp
index ca99121a..a1678b18 100644
--- a/src/renderer/cpu_engine/tvgSwRenderer.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer/cpu_engine/tvgSwRenderer.cpp
@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@ struct SwShapeTask : SwTask
     {
         auto strokeWidth = validStrokeWidth(clipper);
         auto updateShape = flags[0] & (RenderUpdateFlag::Path | RenderUpdateFlag::Transform | RenderUpdateFlag::Clip);
-        auto updateFill = (flags[0] & (RenderUpdateFlag::Color | RenderUpdateFlag::Gradient));
+        auto updateFill = (flags[0] & (RenderUpdateFlag::Color | RenderUpdateFlag::Gradient | RenderUpdateFlag::Transform));
 
         //Shape
         if (updateShape) {
